Oh wait! I bet the issue is that `labor.assigned` in `staffedVisualWorkplaces` is calculated using `laborSectorForBuilding`, and some buildings (like farms) add TWO workers to the demand, but `staffedVisualWorkplaces` only adds ONE worker per building. So there could be a mismatch between the number of workers available and the number of candidate buildings.

