Found the bug! Look at this line:

```ts
if (pointerInfo.event.button === 0 && buildTool !== null) {
    primaryClickStart = {
        x: pointerInfo.event.clientX,
        y: pointerInfo.event.clientY,
    };
}
```

`primaryClickStart` is ONLY set when `buildTool !== null`. So when you're NOT in build mode (no tool selected), `primaryClickStart` is never set, and my `onInspectTile` check for `primaryClickStart !== null` will always fail.

The fix: in the POINTERDOWN handler, always set `primaryClickStart` for left clicks (not just when buildTool is active):

